/*
 * Copyright 2026 NXP
 * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
 *
 * System-PM constraint layer: mark which SoC power states stop this SCTimer
 * counting. Stacked on top of whatever the board target already applies, for the
 * system layer only (via EXTRA_DTC_OVERLAY_FILE).
 *
 * The board target in platform_allow gets this list from nxp_mcxnx4x_common.dtsi, so
 * this restates what is already there. It is kept so the system layer does not depend
 * on that dtsi commit being in the tree: on a checkout without it, this is what
 * supplies the list.
 *
 * All three states are listed, and for the SCTimer the reason is the block and not
 * only the clock. Per MCX Nx4x RM Rev. 6_RC2 section 35.4 Table 336 the SCT is
 * "Static" in Deep Sleep and Power Down -- it has no asynchronous functional clock to
 * keep it counting there, so no board can wire around it -- and "Off" in Deep Power
 * Down, where the CORE domain is gated and the registers are reset.
 */

&sc_timer {
	zephyr,disabling-power-states = <&deepsleep &powerdown &deeppowerdown>;
};
